@startuml collaboration_review
title Figure 10 - Collaboration (Communication) Diagram: One Exception Review\n[Individual task · Member C]\nCSH-02 confirmation difference evaluation (hybrid, L3) in P2: A6 -> JudgmentEngine -> A7 -> A1 -> ReviewQueue -> A10 -> RCA -> A10 -> AuditOutputStore

skinparam defaultFontSize 20
skinparam legendFontSize 20
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam objectBackgroundColor White
skinparam objectBorderColor #444444
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDF0
skinparam noteBorderColor #888800
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 85
hide empty members

' ================= Objects =================
object ":A1 Orchestrator\n(DecisionSubmit, StateQuery)" as A1
object ":RuleEngine" as RE
object ":A6 FieldworkAgent\n(instance fw-L1-2)" as A6
object ":LLMClient\n(main model)" as LLMM
object ":JudgmentEngine\n(owns OutputValidator)" as JE
object ":A7 ReviewAgent" as A7
object ":LLMClient\n(critic model, separate client)" as LLMC
object ":AuditOutputStore" as AOS
object ":ReviewQueue" as RQ
object ":A10 ConciergeAgent" as A10
object "RCA\n(Registered Company Auditor)" as RCA <<human actor>>
object ":EvidenceStore" as ES
object ":AuditTrail" as AT

' ================= Interaction 1: the A6 instance produces the Judgment =================
A1 -- A6 : 1: A1 -> A6  Send(fw-L1-2, EngagementState, procedures\nincl. CSH-02 hybrid L3) -> runProcedure(CSH-02)\n1.13: A6 -> A1  (return) StatePatch: Judgment v1, Exception,\nProcedureRun, ReviewTask draft; A1 sets Procedure\n-> awaiting_human at fan-in

RE -- A6 : 1.1: A6 -> RE  bindParams(rule, engagement), run(rule)\n1.2: RE -> A6  (return) 1 Exception - confirmed balance differs\nfrom the ledger by AUD 142,000; EvidencePointers\n(reply, ledger; no reasoning chain)

LLMM -- A6 : 1.3: A6 -> LLMM  complete(prompt, outputSchema)\n1.4: LLMM -> A6  (return) conclusion, reasoningChain,\ncounterArgument, c_llm

A6 -- JE : 1.5: A6 -> JE  buildJudgment(findings, CSH-02)\n1.6: JE -> A6  (return) Judgment v1, reviewStatus pending\n1.10: A6 -> JE  computeConfidence\n1.11: JE -> A6  (return) 0.87

JE -- JE : 1.5.1: JE -> JE  OutputValidator - syntax, structure,\nreferences, semantics (<= 2 retries)

A6 -- A7 : 1.8: A6 -> A7  independentConclusion(pointers) [r1], compare [r2]\n1.9: A7 -> A6  (return) criticVerdict = consistent, criticReasonType

A7 -- LLMC : 1.8.1: A7 -> LLMC  complete(round 1: pointers only, no chain)\n1.8.2: A7 -> LLMC  complete(round 2: + A6 conclusion)

A6 -- A6 : 1.7: A6 -> A6  gen09Trigger(judgment) -> hit:\ndefault level L3, proposedAction close\n1.12: A6 -> A6  draft ReviewTask (kind normal, target\nJudgment v1 + targetVersion) into the StatePatch\n(override_condition, 7.4: amount above\nperformance_materiality -> effective L1)

A1 -down- RQ : 1.16: A1 -> RQ  publish(ReviewTask)

' ================= Interaction 2: human review through A10 =================
RQ -- A10 : 2: A10 -> RQ  rank()\n2.1: RQ -> A10  (return) ranked ReviewTask + the\ndecisions allowed for its kind (UC-04)

A10 -- RCA : 2.2: A10 -> RCA  present(task) per 9.1 tier - reasoning chain,\nevidence pointers, counter-argument, A7 verdict\n2.3: RCA -> A10  show me the evidence

A10 -- ES : 2.4: A10 -> ES  resolve(pointers: confirmation reply,\nbank statement, ledger line)\n2.5: ES -> A10  (return) Snapshot with coordinate box

A10 -- RCA : 2.6: RCA -> A10  open the reply, the statement\nand the ledger line side by side\n2.7: RCA -> A10  decision = misstatement, misstatementDraft\nAUD 142,000, reason (verbatim, non-empty)

A10 -up- A1 : 2.8: A10 -> A1  submit(ReviewRecord - taskId, targetVersion,\ndecision, payload, reason) via DecisionSubmit

A1 -- A1 : 1.14: A1 -> A1  mergePatch: field authorisation, type,\nid, foreign key -> merged\n2.8.1: A1 -> A1  validate targetVersion, gate state,\nkind x decision matrix (UC-04)\n2.11: A1 -> A1  recompute Procedure -> completed

A1 -down- AOS : 1.15: A1 -> AOS  write(Judgment v1 - confidence 0.87,\ncriticVerdict, reviewStatus pending; Exception; ProcedureRun)\n2.9: A1 -> AOS  write(ReviewRecord); Judgment.reviewStatus -> confirmed\n(a misstatement decision accepts the conclusion, UC-04)\n2.10: A1 -> AOS  write(Misstatement - factual, AUD 142,000)

A10 -- AT : 2.12: A10 -> AT  log(dwell time from 2.2 to 2.7)\nfor the rubber-stamp alarm (9.3)

' ================= Notes =================
note bottom of A7
  A6 -> A7 is the only direct agent-to-agent
  call: a synchronous sub-graph, input =
  evidence pointers and conclusion, output =
  criticVerdict, reason, independent conclusion
  and reasoning chain, not via EngagementState (5.3).
  Two rounds avoid anchoring on the conclusion.
  GEN-09 is evaluated on the default level
  (L3) before the 7.4 downgrade to L1
  (Figure 4b order), so A7 and the human
  both review this Judgment.
end note

note left of RCA
  The human exchanges messages
  only with A10. A10 builds the
  ReviewRecord verbatim: it never
  rewrites the reason and never
  infers approval from the
  conversation (9.5).
end note

note right of RQ
  A6 drafts the ReviewTask, A1 publishes it:
  the task reaches the queue and A10 only
  after mergePatch (18.3.1, 18.4).
  Other outcomes of the same collaboration:
  criticVerdict inconsistent for insufficient
  evidence -> Loop 1 re-run inside A6; still
  inconsistent -> kind dispute, adjudication
  lane; 5% of high-confidence items -> kind blind.
end note

note right of JE
  confidence 0.87 is computed by
  JudgmentEngine from c_ev, c_rule,
  c_llm and c_critic (8.4), never
  taken from the LLM alone.
end note

note bottom of AT
  Every object also writes AuditTrail
  (LLM calls, rule runs, validation
  retries, state transitions); those
  links are omitted. FinancialDataStore
  is omitted too: RuleEngine pushes the
  SQL down to it.
end note

' ================= Layout hints =================
RCA -[hidden]right- AT

legend bottom
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | Object box | Runtime instance, ":Class" or ":Class (instance)"; the <<human actor>> box is the human reviewer |
  | Undirected link | A communication path between two objects; direction is not in the line but in each message label, which names sender -> receiver |
  | n, n.m, n.m.k | Message sequence, nested per UML: messages 1.x are sent while message 1 is being handled |
  | (return) | Reply travelling back along the same link to the sender of the numbered call |
  | Self link | Message an object sends to itself |
  |= Constraint |= |
  | LLM calls | Only A6 (main client) and A7 (critic client, a separate instance); A1, A5 and A9 never call the LLM (5.5) |
  | Human path | RCA <-> A10 only; every decision enters the system as one whole ReviewRecord through DecisionSubmit, validated by A1 (18.5) |
  | Agent path | All other agent traffic travels through A1 as EngagementState patches; A6 -> A7 is the single exception (5.3) |
  | Publication | Agents never write the queue: A6 returns the ReviewTask in its StatePatch, A1 validates and merges it, then publishes (18.3.1) |
  | Scope | Figure 5a shows the planning-phase LLM call chain (A4); this figure shows the fieldwork-phase review collaboration around one Judgment |
endlegend
@enduml
